\\\": \\\"Does the current checkpoint loader enforce complete parameter matching?\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"no\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"current_code.py calls model.load_state_dict(..., strict=False), allowing missing parameters to go unnoticed.\\\"},\n    {\\\"observation\\\": \\\"Does the current script multiply probabilities before export?\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"yes\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"current_code.py assigns test[target_cols] = predictions *100. Positive constant scaling leaves within-label rankings unchanged and is not an AUC improvement.\\\"},\n    {\\\"observation\\\": \\\"Can K-fold model training be validated with the supplied workspace data?\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"no\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The task explicitly states competition data is unavailable and forbids running training/inference. The strategy block was considered once; its training, OOF and loss-weighting recommendations cannot be tested in this inference-only revision.\\\"},\n    {\\\"observation\\\": \\\"Are additional checkpoint files supplied in the current workspace?\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"no\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The local directory listing contains current_code.py, history.md, task.md and prompt.txt, with no checkpoint files. No additional ensemble weights are assumed.\\\"},\n    {\\\"observation\\\": \\\"Are repository-specific AGENTS.md instructions present?\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"no\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"A find restricted to the current directory returned no AGENTS.md files.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"action_summary\\\": \\\"Restore the strongest documented preprocessing: 512-pixel images and standard ImageNet normalization. Preserve horizontal-flip probability averaging and add a conservative full-frame scale ensemble weighted 80% at 512 and 20% at 640, retaining most of the historically stronger scale while adding resolution diversity. This blend is an unvalidated hypothesis; the historical normalization recovery is the main evidence-backed improvement. Keep the supplied checkpoint, model architecture and Kaggle paths; use smaller sequential inference batches, remove unused version-sensitive imports, require complete checkpoint loading, cache scale predictions, and export unscaled probabilities in sample-submission order. No training, inference, external data access or internet use was performed.\\\"\n}\nJSON\npython - <<'PY'\nimport ast\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\ncode = Path('output/revised_code.py').read_text()\nast.parse(code)\nreport = json.loads(Path('output/report.json').read_text())\nassert set(report) == {'observations', 'action_summary'}\nassert isinstance(report['action_summary'], str)\nfor item in report['observations']:\n    assert set(item) == {'observation', 'result', 'evidence'}\n    assert item['result'] in ('yes', 'no')\n    assert all(isinstance(v, str) for v in item.values())\nprint('Python syntax and report schema valid.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Python syntax and report schema valid.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
